QEHECGPFNSCHEWF6AQ5Y3\",\n      \"title\": \"Add merge blocker when review subagent times out\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"notes[0].content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"task\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KHWQEJDNM6BA4KMMC9A7CVPY\",\n      \"title\": \"Review subagent should post structured GitHub review\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"description\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"task\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJ4SMATMC7TD3H0C2S5K9W4T\",\n      \"title\": \"kspec batch cannot handle task patch with nested --data JSON argument. The data object gets stringif\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"notes[4].content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"task\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJBNHZ455RC87A2SYYZ55KV5\",\n      \"title\": \"E2E tests for daemon Tasks API (replace daemon-api-tasks.test.ts)\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"notes[1].content\",\n        \"notes[2].content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"task\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJBNJAPSK8858417YYGBFX7S\",\n      \"title\": \"E2E tests for daemon Error Handling + Projects API (replace 2 files)\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"notes[3].content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"task\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJBNJKVJWSX2240N81H9KYYA\",\n      \"title\": \"Delete static analysis tests for ralph end-loop, web-ui-triage, and misc\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"notes[3].content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"task\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n      \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"notes[7].content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"observation\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KFN35C6AHD2DW8N31ZN1F1T7\",\n      \"title\": \"PR merge blocked by unresolved review threads requiring manual UI action. GitHub API doesn't support programmatic resolution of review conversations - they must be clicked 'Resolve conversation' in the UI. The check-unresolved-comments CI workflow blocks merge even when all issues are fixed and acknowledged by the bot.\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"observation\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KGVCEFG5NP47A9K33GS192PD\",\n      \"title\": \"Codex PR review on self-authored PRs creates review threads that trigger check-unresolved-comments CI gate. Requires manual GraphQL thread resolution + CI re-run before merging. Codex skill should either skip inline comments on own PRs or auto-resolve threads after posting.\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"observation\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJ3X7D52RR2R6N3MS45Y7EE6\",\n      \"title\": \"CI timing race: when Codex posts a review comment after CI check-unresolved-comments has already run, the check fails because the new thread is unresolved. Requires manual re-run after resolving. Consider: (1) make check-unresolved-comments a required-last check, (2) have the review workflow auto-re-run the check after resolving threads, or (3) add a gh run rerun step to the codex review skill.\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"content\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"observation\",\n      \"ulid\": \"01KJD309N30QVB8RRSD7A9J3CV\",\n      \"title\": \"CI check-unresolved-comments timing race in review fix cycle: When Codex posts inline review comments on a PR, we push a fix commit which triggers CI immediately. The check-unresolved-comments job runs BEFORE we resolve the Codex threads via GraphQL, causing it to fail on the new commit. Then requires manual workflow re-run. Mitigation: always resolve all review threads BEFORE pushing any fix commits during a review cycle.\",\n      \"matchedFields\": [\n        \"content\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"total\": 26,\n  \"showing\": 26\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"pattern\": \"check-unresolve